  "scope": "Wake the automatic poll loop on Messages database activity instead of a fixed one-second timer, with a heartbeat fallback.",
  "baseCommit": "7f792f2d7b5f3335ab4c381629ba1e4ecc447815",
  "motivation": "With the persistent Ghostget helper, a poll costs tens of milliseconds, so intake latency is dominated by the timer between polls; polling continuously while idle also spends helper CPU for nothing.",
  "design": {
    "activity": "createMessagesActivity watches the Messages store's chat.db-wal and chat.db files (non-persistent fs watchers) and drops a watcher that reports rename (deleted or moved) and re-arms whenever a file's device/inode changes, so a recreated WAL is watched even when its inode number is reused. It carries no message data: an event only resolves the loop's wait. An unwatchable or absent store falls back to the heartbeat.",
    "schedule": "Automatic loops given an activity source wait for activity or a 3s heartbeat (1s while any contact has sync failures), then tick after a 100ms floor. Activity during a tick is remembered, so a change is never missed between ticks. Without an activity source the loop keeps its one-second timer; tests with automatic:false are unaffected.",
    "unchanged": "Poll, drain, debounce, claim, dispatch, grant and reconciliation logic are unchanged; only when the next poll starts changes."
  },
